<title>CANADA: Canadian union, GM push talks past deadline.</title>
<headline>Canadian union, GM push talks past deadline.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Auto Workers union said it is delaying a midday press conference for three and half hours as tense talks with General Motors Corp continued past a deadline to reach an agreement ending a strike by 26,000 auto workers.</p>
<p>Union officials told reporters that a news conference, originally set for 12.00 p.m eastern time (1600 GMT) would now be held at 3.30 p.m. eastern (1930 GMT).</p>
<p>The union also postponed a caucus meeting set for midday, making it plain that the deadline would not be met. Reporters said GM officials were locked in tense negotiations with CAW president Buzz Hargrove as the deadline passed.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
